# Packages for the ik-os live installer environment. This is NOT the ik-os
# image: it is the throwaway system that runs the installer.
linux-image-amd64
live-boot
systemd-sysv
init
udev
dbus
network-manager
# Wi-Fi in the installer. The live system is bootstrapped from its own list and
# had none of this: NetworkManager was present and could not touch a wireless
# card, which is the only network a laptop has at install time.
#
# The installed image was missing wpasupplicant for the same reason -- it is a
# Recommends, and recommends are off -- which is why a deployed machine saw no
# Wi-Fi networks at all. Both lists have to name it; neither inherits from the
# other.
#
#   network-manager-tui  nmtui, which the installer shells out to. It handles
#                        WPA2/WPA3 passphrases, WPA-Enterprise (802.1X) and
#                        hidden SSIDs, so the installer needs no Wi-Fi UI of
#                        its own and no opinion about the company's auth type.
#   wpasupplicant        NM cannot associate without it. It is only a
#                        Recommends of network-manager, and mmdebstrap does
#                        not install recommends.
#   wireless-regdb       regulatory domains; without it the card is limited to
#                        whatever the driver dares use.
network-manager-tui
wpasupplicant
wireless-regdb
# Firmware, non-free-firmware component (already enabled in build-iso.sh).
# firmware-iwlwifi covers Framework's Intel cards and is 180 MB on its own;
# firmware-misc-nonfree carries the MediaTek firmware the AMD Ryzen models
# need. firmware-realtek is deliberately NOT here: it is another 38 MB and
# Framework ships neither, so a Realtek USB adaptor works on the installed
# system but not during installation. Use a cable for that.
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-misc-nonfree
iproute2
iputils-ping
ca-certificates
bootc-placeholder
# bootc is extracted from the payload image, but its shared libraries are not:
# they come from here, at the same suite as the image so the versions match.
ostree
composefs
# BOOTC_BOOTLOADER=systemd -- bootc needs bootctl and the systemd-boot EFI
# binaries to make the installed disk bootable.
systemd-boot
podman
skopeo
whiptail
parted
gdisk
btrfs-progs
e2fsprogs
dosfstools
# The installer creates the LUKS container itself (ADR 0022), so the live
# system needs cryptsetup. Without it the installer would fail after the
# partition table is already written -- past the point of no return.
cryptsetup
util-linux
kmod
less
nano
zstd
